    },
    {
        "id": 332,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "QUESTION",
        "content": "The least significant bits seem to differ!",
        "choices": [
            {
                "text": "What are least significant bits?",
                "destination_id": 333
            },
            {
                "text": "Nice finding!",
                "destination_id": 345
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": 333,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "Bits are presented as either 0 or 1. A group of eight bits form a byte, which can represent a decimal value between 0 and 255."
    },
    {
        "id": 334,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "QUESTION",
        "content": "The most right bit is the least significant bit, since it adjusts its value minimally.",
        "choices": [
            {
                "text": "Could you give some examples?",
                "destination_id": 335
            },
            {
                "text": "I understand now",
                "destination_id": 345
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": 335,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "The byte 10001000 has a decimal value of 136. Let\u2019s change the least significant bit."
    },
    {
        "id": 336,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "10001000 changed to 10001001, because the most right bit is the least significant bit."
    },
    {
        "id": 337,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "The value of 10001001 is 137, so if this byte represented the colour red, we have only changed its value slightly."
    },
    {
        "id": 338,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "In contrast: if we would have adjusted 10001000 to 00001000, its value would have been 8."
    },
    {
        "id": 339,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "If this byte represented the red colour, the colour would have drastically changed!",
        "next": 345
    },
    {
        "id": 345,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "When we put all the least significant bits of the images behind each other, characters can be read."
    },
    {
        "id": 346,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "Let\u2019s say the number 0 is \u2018a\u2019, and the number 25 is \u2018z\u2019, then we can read a word in the right picture!"
    },
    {
        "id": 347,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "I assume this is the simple protocol that Agent P. came up with."
    },
    {
        "id": 348,
        "character": "Dr. Glitchwell",
        "type": "TEXT",
        "content": "If he used a stego key to randomize which least significant bits are used, we would not be able to have read this message."
